      "is_accepted": true,
      "score": 4,
      "last_activity_date": 1657648889,
      "creation_date": 1657648889,
      "answer_id": 42783,
      "question_id": 42782,
      "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "body": "<p>The <a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/breastfeeding/recommendations/handling_breastmilk.htm\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">CDC</a> has some useful guidelines on this. If you thaw breast milk in the fridge, you can use it within the next 24 hours. Once it is warmed or brought up to room temperature (no matter the method), you should use it within 2 hours. I hope that helps!</p>\n"
